CONTRIBUTING.md
Guidelines for Contributing to the Royal Archer Project
Thank you for your interest in contributing to Royal Archer, 
an editorial studio dedicated to elevating stories, 
nurturing writers, and building tools that support creativity, 
clarity, and craft.
Your participation helps shape a platform where literature, 
education, and digital innovation meet.

🌟 1. Our Mission
Royal Archer exists to support:

editorial and publishing services

creative writing and storytelling

educational courses and articles

digital tools and services for writers and readers

community collaboration and mentorship

future co‑ownership opportunities for long‑term contributors

This repository contains the technical and creative foundations of the Royal Archer ecosystem.
Contributions should strengthen the platform’s quality, clarity, and usefulness.

🛠️ 2. Ways You Can Contribute
We welcome contributions from many disciplines:

Technical Contributions
features, improvements, and bug fixes

digital tools for writers, editors, and learners

automation, integrations, and backend logic

accessibility and performance enhancements

Creative & Editorial Contributions
writing, editing, or refining content

improving clarity, structure, or tone

educational materials, guides, or course modules

translations or language‑support tools

Design Contributions
UI/UX improvements

layout and readability enhancements

visual assets aligned with Royal Archer’s brand

Community Contributions
discussions, proposals, and planning

documentation improvements

feedback on features or content

If you’re unsure whether your idea fits, open an Issue — conversation is part of collaboration.

📬 3. How to Get Started
Step 1 — Fork the Repository
Create your own working copy.

Step 2 — Create a Branch
Use clear, descriptive names such as:
feature/editor-tool, fix/typo, docs/update-guides.

Step 3 — Make Your Changes
Follow the existing style and structure.
Keep your work focused and well‑documented.

Step 4 — Submit a Pull Request (PR)
Include:

a short summary of your changes

why they matter

any notes for review

Your PR will be reviewed by the project owner.

📐 4. Standards & Expectations
To maintain quality:

write clean, readable code

document your changes

keep functions and files focused

maintain consistent tone and style in written content

avoid unnecessary dependencies

ensure accessibility and clarity

For major changes, open an Issue first so we can discuss direction.

🤝 5. Collaboration Culture
Royal Archer values:

clarity

kindness

respect

thoughtful communication

craftsmanship

shared purpose

We build with care — for the work, for each other, and for the writers and readers we serve.

All contributors must follow the project’s Code of Conduct (to be added or linked).

🔐 6. Licensing of Contributions
By contributing, you agree that:

your contribution is your original work

you license it under the MIT License

you accept the additional terms in COLLABORATION‑TERMS.md

contributions do not automatically grant co‑ownership

Ownership of the project remains with Galina B. Nelson unless a separate written agreement is made.

🌱 7. Pathway to Deeper Collaboration
If you wish to become more involved — through long‑term development, 
editorial partnership, or potential future co‑ownership — you are welcome to express your interest.

Co‑ownership is based on:

consistent contribution

shared vision

trust

commitment

alignment with Royal Archer’s mission

A separate written agreement is required for any ownership or revenue‑sharing arrangement.

📣 8. Communication
Use GitHub Issues and Pull Requests for:

questions

proposals

bug reports

feature ideas

discussions

Clear communication helps the project evolve gracefully.

💬 9. Thank You
Your time, creativity, and expertise matter.
Whether you refine a sentence, design a feature, or build a new tool, your 
contribution helps Royal Archer grow into a home for writers, readers, and creators.

We’re building something meaningful — and you’re invited to be part of it.

💬 9. Thank You
Your time, creativity, and expertise matter.
Whether you fix a typo or build a major feature, your contribution helps shape the future of this project.

We’re building something meaningful — and you’re invited to be part of it.
